; Loss-free used_information P6: pc-dependent world SELECTION at a force
; site must be recorded in used_information. The first if widens the shared
; entry's cache to [1.0@b, 2.0@~b] (used = true) through s1. s2's first
; force then HITS that multi-world entry under pc = b; the pc-filter picks
; 1.0, so s2's own entry must carry used = b (the selected world's guard),
; not the entry's blanket true — else s2 goes stale on the ~b branch.
; Correct: b: 1+1 = 2; ~b: 12+12 = 24. Stale s1+s2 (HEAD): 2 / 22.
; Stale s2 only (threading without the guard fold): 2 / 23.
(query
 (let ((b (flip 0.5))
       (m {(if b 1.0 2.0)})
       (s1 (sum m))
       (s2 (sum m)))
   (Posterior (+. (if b s1 (+. s1 10.0))
                  (if b s2 (+. s2 10.0)))
              True)))
